From e0a59093482434b5a9a9d243cd6df08e5ec20da2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:08:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(anthropic): pre-request token check stays on the pinned
 pool account [daveey]

The per-request Anthropic credential check re-resolved "the" token as the first
credential-pool entry and swapped it in whenever it differed. After rotation or
401 recovery had moved a session to account B, every request swapped account A's
(expired) token back; recovery refreshed B, the next pre-check put A back, and after
two refreshes of B the turn gave up ("Non-retryable client error" / fallback model),
burning B's single-use refresh tokens (hermes-hub, 2026-10-27 19:00 PT).

- client_lifecycle: a session pinned to a pool entry (_credential_pool_entry_id)
  only gets that entry's latest token (adopt a peer's persisted rotation, refresh
  when expiring), never another account's. The unpinned path rebinds the entry id to
  the adopted key and warns when that moves the session off its entry.
- anthropic_credentials: model-aware pool resolution skips entries whose access
  token is past its stamped expiry (diagnostic, model-less calls unchanged).
- 401 recovery warns when the failing key belongs to another entry than the one the
  session is attributed to (the signature of this drift).

Regression: tests/agent/test_anthropic_pool_pin.py (7 tests, all red on the base).
